    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is anchored by **Zack Gelof** (66.86) and **Brendan Donovan** (64.97), who emerge as our strongest plays. **Zack Gelof** benefits from a prime matchup against Cody Bradford, with an massive 19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile and a 10% park factor advantage, while **Brendan Donovan** benefits from leading off against Hunter Brown, securing a significant 10% boost for his high-leverage lineup spot. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (62.55) and **Bryce Harper** (62.12) remain lineup locks, with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** maintaining a high floor despite a tough matchup against Casey Mize, buoyed by a +6% order bonus at the heart of the lineup, and **Bryce Harper** continuing to provide elite efficiency with an impressive 0.389 xwOBA.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the final OF spot and our bench depth. **Justin Crawford** (51.68) was the closest candidate to cracking the lineup, but he ultimately remained on the bench because of his projected #9 spot in the order, which carried a -8% penalty that pushed him just behind the higher-upside profiles of **Lawrence Butler** and **Jung Hoo Lee**. While **Dylan Beavers** (57.07) stays in the starting group due to a favorable matchup against Freddy Peralta and the added benefit of attacking a pitcher with a slow delivery, we remain cautious regarding **Yainer Diaz** (40.78), whose score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against Bryan Woo and a projected #9 batting order. Owners should monitor official lineups closely, as the \"Lineup Pending\" status for nearly every player introduces volatility; any shift that bumps **Yainer Diaz** or **Cal Raleigh** further down the order could necessitate a pivot to the bench to preserve our limited game caps.",
